  24:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  25:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****                     ##### GPIO Peripheral features #####
  26:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  27:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  28:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) Each port bit of the general-purpose I/O (GPIO) ports can be
  29:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   individually configured by software in several modes:
  30:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Input mode
  31:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccv05Djj.s 			page 2


  32:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Output mode
  33:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Alternate function mode
  34:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) External interrupt/event lines
  35:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  36:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) During and just after reset, the alternate functions and external
  37:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   interrupt lines are not active and the I/O ports are configured in input
  38:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   floating mode.
  39:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  40:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All GPIO pins have weak internal pull-up and pull-down resistors, which
  41:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   can be activated or not.
  42:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  43:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) In Output or Alternate mode, each IO can be configured on open-drain or
  44:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   push-pull type and the IO speed can be selected depending on the VDD value.
  45:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  46:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The microcontroller IO pins are connected to onboard peripherals/modules
  47:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   through a multiplexer that allows only one peripheral alternate function (AF)
  48:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   connected to an IO pin at a time. In this way, there can be no conflict
  49:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   between peripherals sharing the same IO pin.
  50:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  51:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All ports have external interrupt/event capability. To use external
  52:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   interrupt lines, the port must be configured in input mode. All available GPIO
  53:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   pins are connected to the 16 external interrupt/event lines from EXTI0 to
  54:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   EXTI15.
  55:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  56:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The external interrupt/event controller consists of up to 28 edge
  57:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   detectors (16 lines are connected to GPIO) for generating event/interrupt
  58:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   requests (each input line can be independently configured to select the type
  59:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (interrupt or event) and the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or
  60:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   both). Each line can also be masked independently.
  61:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  62:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****             ##### How to use this driver #####
  63:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  64:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  65:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) Enable the GPIO AHB clock using the following function :
  66:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABLE().
  67:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  68:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) Configure the GPIO pin(s) using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  69:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        (++) Configure the IO mode using "Mode" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef
  70:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   structure
  71:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        (++) Activate Pull-up, Pull-down resistor using "Pull" member from
  72:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  73:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        (++) In case of Output or alternate function mode selection: the speed is
  74:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****              configured through "Speed" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  75:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In alternate mode is selection, the alternate function connected to
  76:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   the IO is configured through "Alternate" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef
  77:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   structure.
  78:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        (++) Analog mode is required when a pin is to be used as ADC channel
  79:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****             or DAC output.
  80:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        (++) In case of external interrupt/event selection the "Mode" member from
  81:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****             GPIO_InitTypeDef structure select the type (interrupt or event) and
  82:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****             the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both).
  83:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  84:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) In case of external interrupt/event mode selection, configure NVIC IRQ
  85:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   priority mapped to the EXTI line using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority() and enable it
  86:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  87:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  88:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) HAL_GPIO_DeInit allows to set register values to their reset value. It's
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccv05Djj.s 			page 3


  89:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   also recommended to use it to unconfigure pin which was used as an external
  90:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   interrupt or in event mode. That's the only way to reset corresponding bit in
  91:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   EXTI & SYSCFG registers.
  92:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  93:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) To get the level of a pin configured in input mode use
  94:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   HAL_GPIO_ReadPin().
  95:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  96:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) To set/reset the level of a pin configured in output mode use
  97:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        HAL_GPIO_WritePin()/HAL_GPIO_TogglePin().
  98:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  99:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) To lock pin configuration until next reset use HAL_GPIO_LockPin().
 100:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
 101:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) During and just after reset, the alternate functions are not
 102:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****        active and the GPIO pins are configured in input floating mode (except
 103:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   JTAG pins).
 104:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
 105:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) The LSE oscillator pins OSC32_IN and OSC32_OUT can be used as general
 106:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   purpose (PC14 and PC15, respectively) when the LSE oscillator is off. The LSE
 107:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   has priority over the GPIO function.
 108:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
 109:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) The HSE oscillator pins OSC_IN/OSC_OUT can be used as
 110:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****         general purpose PF0 and PF1, respectively, when the HSE oscillator is
 111:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c ****   off. The HSE has priority over the GPIO function.
 112:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
